      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For clarity, what roles are you referring to?\n\nRoles only play a part for members of the group itself. A Group Public allows *anyone* to join, and grants moderation ability to the group members (assuming their role has the moderation permission).\n\nSomeone can only have a role if they are a member of the group.\n\nSo, if you limited a Group Public by roles, then you've effectively created a Group instance with role locking, which we already offer.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-08-14T02:03:29.766Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "What if there was a filter to limit which roles can join a group public world? I think this would be an incredible idea to help filter out trolls and kids from instances that can’t use the paid age verification option, or for those who have a hard time moderating.\n\nIt could work like this: when creating the instance, you’d get an option that says, “Which roles would you like to allow in this instance?” Then you could check each role on or off depending on who you want to allow.\n\nThis would fix so many problems in VRChat’s public worlds and could greatly reduce trolling overall. Please consider this idea! This game means a lot to me and my friends, but it’s become so hard to meet people because of the trolling and bad behavior lately.\n\nI hope this reaches you all, and I wish you a great rest of the year!",
